{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And fire went out</b> etc. The fire that went out in the days of Moses did not depart from the copper altar until he came to the eternal house. And that which descended in the days of Solomon did not depart from the altar of burnt offering until it departed in the days of Menasheh."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The last word משה (Moses) appears to be a scribal error for מנשה (Menasheh); translated hyper-literally as written. The chronological logic — fire from Solomon's temple departing in a later king's time — points to Menasheh, and this reading is found in parallel sources."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:58.274487098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}